  "feature1": {
    "prompt": "IterativeImputer currently does not support a fill_value parameter. In many real-world use cases, when the initial_strategy is set to 'constant', it is necessary for the user to supply a constant value for imputation \u2013 similar to what is available in SimpleImputer. The new fill_value parameter should allow a user-defined constant, including the option of np.nan, to be used during the first imputation round. The expected behavior is that when initial_strategy is 'constant', the fill_value provided by the user is correctly propagated and used to replace missing values.",
    "hint_texts": "This feature involves modifying the IterativeImputer class to add a new parameter, fill_value. Specifically, update the __init__ method to accept fill_value and assign it to self.fill_value; update the class docstring and parameter validation to include fill_value details; and modify the _initial_imputation method to pass fill_value to the underlying SimpleImputer. The implementation must mirror the behavior observed in SimpleImputer and allow for np.nan as a valid fill_value.",
